  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Response for Safe, Dignified, and Inclusive Accommodation and Support to Vulnerable IDPs in Dnipropetrovsk Oblast</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe project aims to improve living conditions and access to inclusive services for internally displaced and conflict-affected persons, both for those in communities and residing in collective sites in Dnipropetrovsk oblast &#x2014; one of the priority regions under the UHF 2025 Second Reserve Allocation.ltbrgtThrough a combination of technical adaptation, minor repairs, psychosocial support, and capacity-building, the project will ensure that persons with disabilities, older persons, and individuals with mobility limitations are accommodated in safe, dignified, and accessible conditions.ltbrgtKey activities include:ltbrgt- conducting technical assessments and preparing adaptation designs within minor repairs for collective sitesltbrgt- delivering individualized home-based social assistance and case managementltbrgt- providing psychosocial support through group training programs and individual counselling by psychologists and psychotherapistsltbrgt- organizing inclusion-focused trainings for staff and residents of collective sites.ltbrgtThe project will strengthen the protection environment, enhance community resilience, and promote social inclusion, directly contributing to Strategic Objective 2 of HRP 2025.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
